// go-embedb is a private fork identified by the upstream module path,
// so it has to be routed with a `replace`. It MUST be a module path and
// a pseudo-version, never a filesystem path: a sibling-path replace
// (`../../go-embedb`) resolves only on an operator box that happens to
// have the fork checked out, and it fails in `go mod download` — i.e.
// while loading the module graph, before any build tag or env var is
// read. That is how d0c3c19 took this repo's `main` red with the
// USE_GOEMBEDB flag still defaulted off: the flag cannot gate a
// dependency the module graph needs to resolve. See README.md §Storage.
//
// The repo is PRIVATE, so CI needs credentials to fetch it. They come
// from this repo's own SC registry (`.sc/secrets.yaml`, decrypted with
// the single org-level SC_CONFIG) and reach the Docker build as a buildx
// secret mount — Dockerfile stage `go-builder`.
replace github.com/FerretDB/FerretDB => github.com/simple-container-com/go-embedb v0.0.0-20261125184815-2d8f727d521e

